From d13461aaa1229e047dba350f21c84d0c31a29929 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:40:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ci): upstream sync gate reads jobs once per actionable
 head, on the canonical slug [daveey]

Each gate call read runs/{id}/jobs for every green run in the 50-run list
(oldest first, later runs overwriting), and origin's daveey/hermes slug
answers every REST call with a 301 to example-org/hermes. One
call cost ~100-200 requests of the shared user token and tripped the fleet
GitHub quota brake (worker-6 ledger: 103x jobs 301 + 103x 200 in 3 min).

- candidates() walks runs newest first and reads jobs only for each head's
  newest verdict-bearing run, and only for heads the gate can act on (the
  requested head, recent runs inside the red backoff, heads main lacks).
- Completed run-attempt verdicts are cached on disk ($HERMES_HOME/cache/
  upstream-sync-gate.json), keyed by run id + attempt.
- main() resolves GitHub's name for origin's slug once (known rename map,
  else repos/{slug}.full_name, cached) and calls every endpoint on it.
- The run list reads one page (page=1: the newest 50 runs, as documented);
  github_pages no longer --paginates an endpoint that names its page, which
  walked the whole run history (63 runs = 2 pages, growing).

Live read-only probe on worker-3 against example-org/hermes:
candidates() made 2 requests (run list + 1 jobs read) for 49 heads.
